.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1104 AM PDT Fri Oct 23 2026

Satellite imagery is messy this morning, depicting a mix of clear
skies but also MVFR to VFR ceilings across the region. You can see
some drier air that worked its way through, eroding stratus as it
moves south but behind it clouds sink in from the northeast. Models
aren`t capturing this that well so opted to keep the general trends
from the prior forecast and with VFR conditions by 20-21Z for most
sites. Then skies will continue to clear as drier air continues to
work into the region, leaving us with VFR conditions into tomorrow
morning. There could be an exception for patchy fog in the North Bay
Valleys around sunrise tomorrow given lingering moisture and the
potential for radiational fog. But it`ll have to compete against
the drier air and weak offshore flow, so opted to keep conditions
clear.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR conditions are expected at SFO; however, there
could be a couple of more hours of MVFR cigs trying to sneak their
way through as some clouds move in from the northeast. SKies should
clear during the late afternoon or early evening hours and be
accompanied with breezy onshore winds. Overnight and into Saturday
morning, light offshore winds are expected with onshore flow
returning mid to late Saturday afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...The morning stratus has eroded with
stratocu blossoming behind it. This will leave us right around or
just above VFR cigs for the next couple of hours, with skies
clearing later this afternoon and into the evening. Overnight, light
offshore winds develop keeping us VFR for through Saturday
morning.

