.MARINE...
(Today through Wednesday)
Issued at 915 AM PDT Fri Oct 23 2026

Conditions will continue to dry out this morning and be
accompanied with fresh to locally strong northerly winds. Near
gale force to gale force gusts possible across the far northern
outer waters, with strong gusts south of Pigeon Point. Winds will
gradually decrease through the day leading to moderate northerly
breeze by Saturday morning and then prevailing through the
upcoming week. Rough seas are expected today and tomorrow across
the outer waters with wave heights peaking between 10 to 13 feet.
Moderate seas prevail Sunday through much of next week.

